              "thumbnail": "/scenes/iapetus/iapetus-normal-thumbnail.webp",
              "surface": "iapetus-normal-surface@2x.webp",
              "poles": "iapetus-normal-poles@2x.webp",
              "source": {
                "id": "cassini-voyager-2008-iapetus",
                "path": "../manifest.json"
              },
              "summary": "Polar detail is coarse compared with the rest of the surface. Photographed shadows and seams remain; the grid marks gaps."
            },
            {
              "id": "enhanced",
              "label": "Enhanced color",
              "description": "Published 2014 enhanced-color Cassini composite, photometrically corrected by Paul Schenk, with nominal 400 m source pixels. Colors extend into ultraviolet and infrared. The dark leading hemisphere is real surface albedo, not a shadow or missing imagery. All supplied pixels are preserved; coarse patches and residual photographed shading remain. Shared Shadows and globe lighting remain active; shape is approximated by a sphere.",
              "title": "Enhanced-color composite",
              "thumbnail": "/scenes/iapetus/iapetus-enhanced-thumbnail.webp",
              "surface": "iapetus-enhanced-surface@2x.webp",
              "poles": "iapetus-enhanced-poles@2x.webp",
              "source": {
                "id": "cassini-iss-2014-iapetus-color",
                "path": "../manifest.json"
              },
              "summary": "Colors extend into infrared and ultraviolet. The dark leading hemisphere is real surface material, not missing imagery."
            },
            {
              "id": "infrared",
              "label": "Infrared",
              "description": "Three Cassini VIMS observations from 10 September 2007. False color assigns red to about 2.02 µm, green to 1.59 µm and blue to 1.28 µm. All three channels share a 0–0.45 I/F display range and gamma 2.2; this stretch changes the display only. No photometric correction is applied, so illumination remains. Archive noise filtering and local replacement are retained; original detector defects and potentially affected neighbors are excluded. Gray grid marks unsupported areas and scan gaps.",
              "summary": "Cassini false color: red 2.02, green 1.59, blue 1.28 µm. Coverage is partial; gray grid marks gaps. Illumination and archive filtering remain in these uncorrected measurements.",
              "title": "Cassini VIMS flyby spectra · 10 September 2007",
              "thumbnail": "/scenes/iapetus/iapetus-infrared-thumbnail.webp",
              "surface": "iapetus-infrared-surface@2x.webp",
              "poles": "iapetus-infrared-poles@2x.webp",
              "source": {
                "id": "iapetus-cassini-infrared",
                "path": "../manifest.json",
                "url": "https://vims.univ-nantes.fr/cube/1568157352_4"
              },
              "detail": "Partial VIMS",
              "falseColor": true
            },
            {
              "id": "ice-absorption",
              "label": "Ice absorption",
              "description": "Near-2.02 µm water-ice band depth relative to a linear 1.82–2.20 µm continuum, using three Cassini VIMS observations from 10 September 2007. This measures absorption strength, not ice abundance. Viewing angle, grain size and noise also affect the values; no photometric correction is applied. Archive noise filtering and local replacement remain; original detector defects and potentially affected neighbors are excluded. Display colors saturate outside 0–0.8; original numerical values are retained. Gray grid marks unsupported areas and scan gaps.",
              "summary": "Near-2.02 µm water-ice absorption in partial Cassini coverage. Gray grid marks gaps. Viewing angle, grain size, noise and archive filtering affect these uncorrected values; they do not measure ice abundance.",
              "title": "Cassini VIMS flyby water-ice absorption · 10 September 2007",
              "thumbnail": "/scenes/iapetus/iapetus-ice-absorption-thumbnail.webp",
